<h3 id="3-behavior-records-on-high-school-transcripts">3. Behavior Records on High School Transcripts</h3>

<p>Additionally, some schools may choose to include notes about your attendance or disciplinary records on your transcript. While policies vary, these behavioral details can provide additional context about your overall engagement and conduct during your high school years.</p>

<p>Now, it’s important to note that these behavioral records are not always included, and their weight in the admissions or hiring process can vary. However, if they are present, it’s a good idea to review them carefully to ensure they accurately reflect your high school experience.</p>

<p>For instance, if you had a few unexcused absences due to a family emergency, you may want to provide an explanation to admissions officers or potential employers. By offering context, you can help them understand the circumstances surrounding any blemishes on your transcript and reassure them of your reliability and commitment.</p>

